course: dictionary
lesson: 9938
title: Tarantulas: big, hairy and shy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tarantula is a large, hairy spider that lives in warm places, such as deserts and rainforests. Some people keep tarantulas as pets. When you read about one, the words around it tell you what it is like.
explain: «Tarantulas are mostly gentle; their bite is usually no worse than a bee sting.» The word gentle and the comparison to a bee sting tell you that a tarantula is usually not dangerous to people. Stories often make tarantulas seem scary, but in real life they are shy.
explain: Counting legs helps you sort animals. «Ants, beetles, mantises and cockroaches have six legs and are insects, while tarantulas and scorpions have eight and are relatives of spiders.» So a tarantula is not an insect, even though it is a small animal with a hairy body.
fact: A tarantula is a large, hairy spider.
fact: Tarantulas have eight legs and two body parts.
fact: «Tarantulas» live in warm places, such as deserts and rainforests in the Americas, Africa, Asia and Australia.
fact: Most tarantulas hunt insects at night, and many live in burrows.
fact: Some tarantulas flick tiny itchy hairs when they are scared, to defend themselves.
exercise: «Tarantulas are mostly gentle; their bite is usually no worse than a bee sting.» What does this sentence tell us about a tarantula bite? | It is like a snake bite | *It is usually no worse than a bee sting | It never happens | It is always deadly
exercise: What is a tarantula? | A small insect with six legs | *A large, hairy spider | A type of beetle | A kind of snake that lives in the sea
exercise: «Counting legs sorts them out.» How many legs does a tarantula have? | Ten | Four | *Eight | Six
test: «Most tarantulas hunt at night and many live in burrows.» Where would a tarantula most likely spend the day? | In the open sea | In a glass of water | On a bright snowy mountain top | *In a burrow in the ground
test: Ants, beetles and mantises are insects. Which animal in this list is NOT an insect? | *Tarantula | Ant | Beetle | Mantis
exam: Which fact about a tarantula is true? | It lives only in cold places | *Its bite is usually no worse than a bee sting | It has six legs like an ant | It always attacks people on sight
